WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.959
Week 35: Analysis, Argument, and Professional Listening. identify main idea and supporting detail defend an opinion summarize unfamiliar material

2
00:00:10.959 --> 00:00:22.004
Cultural lens. Professional topics include society, economy, environment, public policy, science, and security without requiring specialist jargon.

3
00:00:22.004 --> 00:00:34.182
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:46.211
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:46.211 --> 00:00:55.231
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:55.231 --> 00:01:30.812
Model language. Los temas profesionales incluyen sociedad y economía. — Professional topics include society and economy. También incluyen medio ambiente y política pública. — They also include environment and public policy. La ciencia y la seguridad son temas comunes. — Science and security are common topics. Se puede hablar de esto sin necesitar jerga especializada. — You can discuss this without needing specialized jargon. Cada tema se puede abordar con claridad. — Each topic can be addressed clearly.

7
00:01:30.812 --> 00:01:40.817
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
